// H6e: Kabootar bytecode VM subset — thin facade (impl in vm_run.kab).
// import "self_host/vm_impl" (used internally by self_host/vm.kab)
//
// Re-export by alias (not a wrapping fn): a wrapping `fn runModuleImpl` adds an extra
// host `call_value` frame. Under KABOOTAR_VM=kab-only that breaks reentrancy of module
// `vGlobals` when the outer probe is self-host-compiled (lets → globals) and a nested
// guest has imports — see self_host/vm.kab header for the full explanation (that
// facade re-exports this one's `runModuleImpl` again as `runModule`).
//
// vm_run.kab stays skip-listed: self-host-compiling its ~27KB body (runOpMem/Arith/
// Cmp/Data/Jump/Call/Ctrl dispatch plus runFnBody/runMethodBody/vNewInstance) is too
// slow for CI. Its ~15 top-level fns all share module-level interpreter state
// (vStack, vLocals, vGlobals, vClasses, …) via plain call/return — not via imports —
// so it cannot be sharded across files without breaking that shared mutable state
// (Kabootar modules don't share globals across files: each import gets its own copy
// of exported bindings). This facade's own source is a two-line import + alias, so
// `compile self_host/vm_impl.kab --self-host` is CI-fast regardless of vm_run.kab.

import "self_host/vm_run"

pub let runModuleImpl = runModuleImplCore
